meta {
  name: Interface - Get
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/workflows/:workflow/interface
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
  workflow: {{workflowId}}
}

docs {
  The workflow's input contract — the fields a run expects. Requires the
  `workflow.view` permission.

  This is what makes a workflow usable by someone who didn't build it:
  without an interface, "run this workflow" means "post the right arbitrary
  JSON", which only its author knows.

  The contract is either declared through `Interface - Update` or, when no
  declaration exists, derived from the graph. The response also carries
  `workflow_id` and `published`.

  Response is wrapped:
  `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { interface } }`.
}
